# issuer_private.pem stays ignored (absent here). organizer_nostr.json + limits.json ARE
# committed for the shared TEST setup so the organizer key + community code stay consistent
# across machines. NOTE: organizer_nostr.json holds a BURNT test key (derived from a documented
# public seed — see its "_seed"/"_notice" fields; anyone can recompute it) — testing only. A REAL
# deployment's organizer_nostr.json must NEVER be committed; see the root .gitignore rule for it.
issuer_private.pem
issuer_public.pem
relay_onion.txt
relay_ws.txt
dashboard_auth/
tag_policy.json
guide.json
invites.json
mailbox_seen.json
storage.json

# Content-epoch symmetric keys (K_E, rotating — seals post bodies). SECRET key material: a leak lets
# anyone decrypt community content. Written at runtime by contentEpochWatcher; NEVER commit.
content_epochs.json

# Per-member per-epoch draw ledger — the double-spend state that meters token draws. Runtime state
# (machine-specific, reveals member draw activity); NEVER commit.
draws.json

# Seeded private bridge lines (T14) — the organizer's per-deployment obfs4/webtunnel bridges;
# runtime state, NEVER commit (leaking them burns the bridges).
bridges.json

# Community relay mirrors (stiq:mirrors) — the organizer's own additional relay operators for the
# community; runtime state, NEVER commit (like bridges.json, not part of the shared TEST setup).
mirrors.json

# Encrypted community-archive exports (T16-S5). Even encrypted, keep the blob out of the repo —
# it concentrates every community secret behind only a passphrase.
*.stiqarch

# Token domain-separation purpose keys (minted when STIQ_TOKEN_DOMAIN_SEP=1) — NEVER commit.
# Glob covers ALL purposes (post/read, picture/audio write+read, space-write, and any future one):
# the earlier explicit list silently missed the four media key files.
*_token_key_private.pem
*_token_key_public.b64
